# RISC0 Proof Generation and Verification Standards

## Context
- When implementing or modifying RISC0 proof generation code
- When handling proof compression and verification
- When managing proof lifecycle from generation to submission

## Requirements

### Proof Generation
- Log detailed metrics at each stage of proof generation:
  - Memory image details (ID, size, pages)
  - Input configuration and sizes
  - Execution environment setup
  - Session execution status
  - Prover initialization
  - Proof statistics (segments, cycles)

### Error Handling
- Implement comprehensive error handling with context:
  - Session execution failures
  - Prover initialization errors
  - Proof generation failures
  - Receipt conversion errors
  - Identity proof failures
  - Compression failures

### Proof Compression
- Validate architecture requirements before compression
- Log compression process details:
  - Tool paths and existence
  - Input/output file details
  - Execution status of external tools
  - Final proof size and format

### Proof Verification
- Track and log proof metadata:
  - Exit codes (system and user)
  - Component sizes
  - Execution digests
  - Receipt structure

### Metrics and Monitoring
- Emit histograms for key metrics:
  - Proof segments
  - Total cycles
  - User cycles
  - Image compute estimates
  - Download sizes

## Examples

### Good Example - Proof Generation
```rust
info!(
    "Starting proof generation:\n\
     - Image ID: {}\n\
     - Memory image size: {} pages\n\
     - Number of inputs: {}", 
    image_id,
    memory_image.pages.len(),
    sorted_inputs.len()
);

let info = match prover.prove_session(&ctx, &session) {
    Ok(info) => {
        info!("Proof generation successful");
        info!(
            "Proof stats:\n\
             - Segments: {}\n\
             - Total cycles: {}\n\
             - User cycles: {}", 
            info.stats.segments,
            info.stats.total_cycles,
            info.stats.user_cycles
        );
        info
    }
    Err(e) => {
        error!("Proof generation failed: {}", e);
        return Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Proof generation failed: {}", e));
    }
};
```

### Bad Example - Insufficient Logging
```rust
// Don't do this - lacks proper logging and error context
let info = prover.prove_session(&ctx, &session)?;
let receipt = info.receipt;
return Ok(receipt);
```

### Good Example - Error Handling with Context
```rust
if let InnerReceipt::Composite(cr) = &info.receipt.inner {
    info!("Converting composite receipt to succinct receipt");
    let sr = match prover.composite_to_succinct(&cr) {
        Ok(sr) => {
            info!("Succinct receipt conversion successful");
            sr
        }
        Err(e) => {
            error!("Failed to convert to succinct receipt: {}", e);
            return Err(anyhow::anyhow!("Failed to convert to succinct receipt: {}", e));
        }
    };
} else {
    error!("Expected composite receipt");
    return Err(Risc0RunnerError::ProofGenerationError.into());
}
```

### Bad Example - Poor Error Handling
```rust
// Don't do this - lacks error context and logging
let sr = prover.composite_to_succinct(&cr)?;
let receipt = identity_p254(&sr)?;
return Ok(receipt);
``` 